0,Akpet language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Akpet_language,"Akpet, also known as Ukpet-Ehom or Akpet-Ehom, is a dialect cluster of the Upper Cross River languages of Nigeria. The varieties are Ukpet (Akpet) and Ehom (Ubeteng, Ebeteng).",Ukpet-Ehom,Niger-Congo
1,Ukpet-Ehom Language (AKD) – L1 & L2 Speakers... | Ethnologue Free,https://www.ethnologue.com/language/akd/,"Ukpet-Ehom is an endangered indigenous language of Nigeria. It belongs to the Niger-Congo language family. The language is used as a first language by all adults in the ethnic community, but not all young people.",Ukpet-Ehom,Niger-Congo
2,Ukpet-Ehom - akd (Niger-Congo) - PeopleGroups.org,https://peoplegroups.org/language/akd/,"Language Profile. Ukpet-Ehom (akd). Ukpet-Ehom (akd) is part of the Niger-Congo family and Niger-Congo, Atlantic-Congo, Volta-Congo, Benue-Congo, Cross River, Delta Cross, Upper Cross, Akpet class.",Ukpet-Ehom,Niger-Congo
